   21: Two execution paths, same outputs:
   22: - in-RAM (default): per-chunk partial reduce with min/max positions,
   23:   one global final merge. Holds ~28 B/accumulator-entry ג€” fine to ~1B
   24:   entries on the 63 GB box.
   25: - two-pass disk spill (spill_dir= set AND raw hits >= spill_min_hits):
   26:   the full corpus emits ~4-5B raw hits; position records would need
   27:   ~126 GB, over the box's free disk. Pass 1 spills only (pair-key u8,
   28:   count u2) records (10 B/entry) hash-partitioned by page pair, then
   29:   reduces each partition independently -> candidate segments
   30:   (pair, bucket_lo, bucket_hi, count). Pass 2 re-emits the same hits
   31:   (deterministic: same gram tables, same chunk bounds) and recovers
